From: balena-seeed-rockchip integration
Subject: [PATCH] IspFec: give rk_ispfec_api_vb_init its fd parameter in the header

src/rk_ispfec_videobuf.c defines rk_ispfec_api_vb_init(int fd) but
rk_ispfec_videobuf.h declares it with an empty parameter list; GCC 14
rejects the conflicting types.  Declare the parameter the definition
already takes (the other three vb APIs in the same header already
carry their fd parameter).

Upstream-Status: Submitted [needed by any GCC>=14 build of the rkaiq-2025_08_11 tree]
Signed-off-by: qian
---
 IspFec/include/rk_ispfec_videobuf.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/IspFec/include/rk_ispfec_videobuf.h b/IspFec/include/rk_ispfec_videobuf.h
--- a/IspFec/include/rk_ispfec_videobuf.h
+++ b/IspFec/include/rk_ispfec_videobuf.h
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ struct rkfec_buffer {
     uint64_t size;
     void* map;
 };

-int rk_ispfec_api_vb_init();
+int rk_ispfec_api_vb_init(int fd);
 void rk_ispfec_api_vb_deinit(int fd);
 int rk_ispfec_api_vb_alloc(int fd, uint32_t size, struct rkfec_buffer* buf);
 int rk_ispfec_api_vb_free(int fd, struct rkfec_buffer* buf);
--
2.34.1

